{"term":"yearn","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a592228751beaac952","definition":"To have a strong desire for something or to do something; to long for or to do something.","example":"All I yearn for is a simple life.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["pant","salivate","burn"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9dc5414d9fa5bc8193","definition":"Of music, words, etc.: to express strong desire or longing.","example":"The music, yearning like a God in pain, / She scarcely heard: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a605e040e3f8d3f220","definition":"To have strong feelings of affection, love, sympathy, etc., toward someone.","example":"And Joſeph made haſte: for his bowels did yerne upon his brother: and he ſought where to weepe, and hee entred into his chamber, & wept there.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated, intransitive","wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:406ddf194fba679b07","definition":"To be distressed or pained; to grieve; to mourn.","example":"My father’s and my uncle Toby’s hearts yearn’d with ſympathy for the poor fellow’s 