ially in the cheesemaking process.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Northern-England, Scotland","register":"Northern-England, Scotland, transitive","wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d27ca8229b2f0ac129","definition":"To make (cheese) from curdled milk.","example":"Also his Honour the Duke will accept ane of our Dunlop cheeses, and it sall be my faut if a better was ever yearned in Lowden.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Northern-England, Scotland","register":"Northern-England, Scotland, transitive","wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/jɜːn/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7f/En-us-yearn.ogg/En-us-yearn.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["yearner","yearnful","yearning","yearnly","yearnsome","yearny"]}